<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Virbhadra Singh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1934–2021</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Virbhadra Singh was the last Raja of the princely state of Bashahr in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himalayas">Himalaya</a> and an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-national-congress">Indian National Congress</a> politician. After the state merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> he served six terms as Chief Minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himachal-pradesh">Himachal Pradesh</a> between 1983 and 2017, as well as a member of parliament and union minister.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/virbhadra-singh.jpg" alt="Virbhadra Singh" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Snjsharma · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Virbhadra_Singh_HP.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
